generated from its native values; BHHCert/TrigTabLitCheck.lean proves that both agree at every grid point (one kernel check),
so `cosSinTabLit = cosSinTab` (`cosSinTabLit_eq`) and `CosSinSound cosSinTabLit` follows from `cosSinTab_sound`
(BHH/TrigTabLit.lean). A lookup walks at most 28 + 63 list cells, instead of evaluating `cosSin` at the grid point
(26 Taylor terms and four doublings) in every declaration that needs it.
